1
00:00:00,711 --> 00:00:06,709
[A Bona Fide Killer]

2
00:00:08,716 --> 00:00:09,716
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09,716 --> 00:00:10,716
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10,716 --> 00:00:11,716
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:12,796 --> 00:00:15,181
[Episode 6]

6
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:23,106
Just how far is he going?

7
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:28,373
I've been here before.

8
00:00:28,373 --> 00:00:30,021
What? When?

9
00:00:30,021 --> 00:00:31,946
Where is this place, Mr. Kwon?

10
00:00:35,749 --> 00:00:37,717
Wait, a casino?

11
00:00:37,717 --> 00:00:40,777
Chairman Cheon came to a casino
at a time like this?

12
00:00:40,777 --> 00:00:44,446
When two people just died
at his construction site?

13
00:00:56,661 --> 00:00:59,280
Chairman, I'm Kwon Tae Seong
from Not Today. I requested an interview.

14
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:01,180
Wait, just a moment...

15
00:01:02,169 --> 00:01:03,502
Why are you covering my mouth?

16
00:01:03,502 --> 00:01:04,853
Chairman! Just a moment.

17
00:01:04,853 --> 00:01:07,322
Wait, Chairman!

18
00:01:07,322 --> 00:01:08,580
Just a moment.

19
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:10,846
Just let me in for a moment!

20
00:01:12,513 --> 00:01:13,901
I told you to stop.

21
00:01:13,901 --> 00:01:15,613
Stay put.

22
00:01:27,605 --> 00:01:28,689
Are you okay, Mr. Kwon?

23
00:01:28,689 --> 00:01:29,857
Yeah. You got it, right?

24
00:01:29,857 --> 00:01:31,993
Oh, yes, I got it.

25
00:01:31,993 --> 00:01:34,665
Still, it was worth following him
all the way here.

26
00:01:34,665 --> 00:01:38,057
Just coming to a casino
at a time like this is newsworthy.

27
00:01:38,057 --> 00:01:40,729
- That's not enough, though, huh?
- What?

28
00:01:40,729 --> 00:01:43,713
Not everyone at a casino is there to gamble.

29
00:01:43,713 --> 00:01:45,413
We need to catch him actually gambling,

30
00:01:45,413 --> 00:01:47,761
or at least meet him
and get a few words out of him.

31
00:01:47,761 --> 00:01:49,461
We came all this way for this.

32
00:01:51,693 --> 00:01:52,693
But how are we supposed to do that?

33
00:01:52,693 --> 00:01:55,629
They don't even look like they'll let us
take one step inside, do they?

34
00:01:55,629 --> 00:01:57,680
Is this the only way in?

35
00:02:01,781 --> 00:02:03,880
<i>Go through the lobby,
pass the bell desk on the left,</i>

36
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:06,146
<i>and open the door on the right.</i>

37
00:02:07,781 --> 00:02:10,413
<i>There should be a staff-only elevator.</i>

38
00:02:15,646 --> 00:02:18,080
<i>Take it to the maid's room on B3</i>

39
00:02:18,829 --> 00:02:21,213
and get a master key for the rooms.

40
00:02:23,121 --> 00:02:24,593
Could I ask you a favor?

41
00:02:24,593 --> 00:02:26,580
Of course, I have to help.

42
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:30,237
You're investigating a case
involving an unjust death, after all.

43
00:02:30,237 --> 00:02:35,725
Your article helped us a lot when we were
fighting wrongful dismissal last year.

44
00:02:35,725 --> 00:02:38,749
Come this way, through the back door.
Come with me.

45
00:02:42,085 --> 00:02:44,180
Excuse me.

46
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:48,413
<i>Doors closing.</i>

47
00:02:52,057 --> 00:02:53,729
What floor?

48
00:02:53,729 --> 00:02:56,177
B3, the parking garage.

49
00:02:56,177 --> 00:02:58,046
This is for staff only.

50
00:02:58,046 --> 00:03:02,213
You'll have to go back up to the first floor
and take the elevator outside.

51
00:03:02,213 --> 00:03:03,880
Oh, okay. Got it. I'm sorry.

52
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,580
Oh, okay.

53
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:12,446
<i>Doors closing.</i>

54
00:03:19,601 --> 00:03:21,181
Looks like you won't
need to go to the maid room.

55
00:03:21,181 --> 00:03:23,713
Just go straight up to the 23rd floor.

56
00:03:29,517 --> 00:03:31,946
Reporting with you...

57
00:03:32,757 --> 00:03:34,846
is always thrilling.

58
00:03:38,477 --> 00:03:40,980
You'll get used to it eventually.

59
00:03:41,732 --> 00:03:45,146
<i>It seems like it'll be
hard to go up unnoticed.</i>

60
00:03:45,146 --> 00:03:48,980
There are two maids on B1
and two more on the first floor.

61
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:50,580
Just avoid showing your face
as much as possible.

62
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:51,813
I'll delete the footage right away.

63
00:03:51,813 --> 00:03:53,546
<i>Okay.</i>

64
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,746
- <i>Doors closing.</i>
- Why is it so exhausting today?

65
00:04:22,489 --> 00:04:23,680
I don't know why there's
so much going on today.

66
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,557
Seriously, why is there so darn much work?

67
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,257
I'm exhausted.

68
00:04:28,185 --> 00:04:31,313
Oh? You're VIP guests.

69
00:04:31,313 --> 00:04:33,889
Oh, I think you got on the wrong elevator.

70
00:04:33,889 --> 00:04:35,113
What?

71
00:04:35,113 --> 00:04:38,513
Next time, use the VIP elevator
on the other side of the hall.

72
00:04:38,513 --> 00:04:40,780
This one's for staff.

73
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,833
Oh, I see.

74
00:04:42,833 --> 00:04:44,953
Thank you.

75
00:04:44,953 --> 00:04:46,653
You too, ma'am.

76
00:04:58,461 --> 00:05:00,161
[Yul's Daycare]

77
00:05:19,961 --> 00:05:22,780
Excuse me, I'm getting off.

78
00:05:37,921 --> 00:05:40,465
What's wrong?

79
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:42,725
Huh?

80
00:05:42,725 --> 00:05:44,033
Never mind.

81
00:05:44,033 --> 00:05:46,446
Her back just looked like someone.

82
00:05:47,609 --> 00:05:48,817
What a crazy punk.

83
00:05:48,817 --> 00:05:51,413
No, I mean, me.

84
00:05:57,169 --> 00:05:59,461
Yes, Miss. How are you?

85
00:05:59,461 --> 00:06:02,869
Sorry, I couldn't answer your call.
What is it about?

86
00:06:02,869 --> 00:06:05,017
<i>Oh, it's nothing serious.</i>

87
00:06:05,017 --> 00:06:07,657
I'm calling about Yul's first-semester
parent consultation.

88
00:06:07,657 --> 00:06:10,989
<i>You didn't reply in the app to let us know</i>

89
00:06:10,989 --> 00:06:13,703
whether you'd prefer a phone
or in-person consultation.

90
00:06:13,703 --> 00:06:19,169
Oh, sorry. I missed that.
Well, I'll do the in-person consultation.

91
00:06:19,169 --> 00:06:22,380
<i>Yes, thank you, Miss. Yes.</i>

92
00:06:26,413 --> 00:06:29,357
Yeah, I'll take the stairs from here.

93
00:06:29,357 --> 00:06:31,361
<i>Watch for anyone coming in.</i>

94
00:06:31,361 --> 00:06:33,265
We can't have any more witnesses.

95
00:06:33,265 --> 00:06:35,913
Okay, Ms. Yoo, I'll keep a close watch.

96
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:44,746
How can I help you?

97
00:06:44,746 --> 00:06:47,757
Are you here as a guest?

98
00:06:47,757 --> 00:06:51,157
I'm not here to gamble.
I'm here to meet someone.

99
00:06:51,157 --> 00:06:53,080
Who are you looking for?

100
00:06:53,683 --> 00:06:56,780
Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
of Gaecheon Construction is inside, right?

101
00:06:58,519 --> 00:07:01,097
Did you make an appointment?

102
00:07:01,097 --> 00:07:03,613
He'll know me if you tell him Kwon Tae Seong.

103
00:07:04,311 --> 00:07:07,648
<i>There are guards stationed
on every floor of the VIP rooms.</i>

104
00:07:07,648 --> 00:07:10,473
<i>When I give you the signal,
come out and move to the left.</i>

105
00:07:10,473 --> 00:07:12,173
Okay.

106
00:07:17,189 --> 00:07:18,889
Now!

107
00:07:24,213 --> 00:07:26,280
When's the next shift coming?

108
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:47,245
I'm in.

109
00:07:47,245 --> 00:07:48,945
This is a nice room.

110
00:07:49,577 --> 00:07:52,080
Wow, what a view.

111
00:07:53,413 --> 00:07:55,040
<i>It's annoying, right?</i>

112
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,745
A guy who should be in a prison cell.

113
00:07:56,745 --> 00:07:58,613
I'll head over to the fridge.

114
00:08:27,861 --> 00:08:29,185
- Done.
- Put it back in the fridge

115
00:08:29,185 --> 00:08:30,846
and take everything else out.

116
00:08:30,846 --> 00:08:33,605
Just leave that one bottle of water.

117
00:08:33,605 --> 00:08:36,057
<i>I saw on social media that Tak Jong Gu
is an "iced drink till I die" guy.</i>

118
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:39,646
What's that?
Something like "a punch in the face"?

119
00:08:41,981 --> 00:08:44,089
Well, that's not bad either.

120
00:08:44,089 --> 00:08:47,646
<i>It means he only drinks iced beverages.</i>

121
00:08:54,745 --> 00:08:56,445
Done.

122
00:08:59,045 --> 00:09:00,745
I'm heading out.

123
00:09:02,677 --> 00:09:04,380
<i>Wait, Ms. Yoo.</i>

124
00:09:05,957 --> 00:09:08,513
Someone's coming down the hall.

125
00:09:08,513 --> 00:09:10,313
<i>Looks like guests.</i>

126
00:09:10,313 --> 00:09:13,597
One man and one woman.

127
00:09:13,597 --> 00:09:15,297
It's Tak Jong Gu.

128
00:09:18,233 --> 00:09:20,157
That woman is...

129
00:09:20,157 --> 00:09:22,280
Huh? A liquor bottle?

130
00:09:24,209 --> 00:09:26,109
First time somewhere this fancy?

131
00:09:26,109 --> 00:09:27,809
Yeah.

132
00:09:28,725 --> 00:09:30,965
Come on in.

133
00:09:30,965 --> 00:09:34,113
- This is my room.
- Wow!

134
00:09:35,633 --> 00:09:38,413
This room is incredible.

135
00:09:40,613 --> 00:09:43,249
You really were born
to the right parents, huh?

136
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:46,557
Aren't the rooms...

137
00:09:46,557 --> 00:09:48,373
non-smoking?

138
00:09:48,373 --> 00:09:50,181
What's not allowed?

139
00:09:50,181 --> 00:09:53,529
If anyone acts up,
I can just throw money at them.

140
00:09:53,529 --> 00:09:56,946
Man, the more I see you, the more I like you.

141
00:10:00,609 --> 00:10:03,101
<i>That's the woman. Today's variable.</i>

142
00:10:03,101 --> 00:10:06,517
She's the one who snatched
my VIP pass at the gaming room.

143
00:10:06,517 --> 00:10:08,405
What's the variable this time?

144
00:10:08,405 --> 00:10:10,213
I'm not sure about that either...

145
00:10:10,213 --> 00:10:12,521
<i>He's supposed to be stuck
in the gaming room until dawn.</i>

146
00:10:12,521 --> 00:10:14,546
But why are those two here at this hour...

147
00:10:15,441 --> 00:10:19,313
<i>If you stay hidden there,
I'll find a way to get you out.</i>

148
00:10:24,421 --> 00:10:27,765
Won't they figure out we lied right away?

149
00:10:27,765 --> 00:10:29,213
Well, it's not exactly a lie.

150
00:10:29,213 --> 00:10:32,997
I said he'd know my name.
I never said I had an appointment.

151
00:10:32,997 --> 00:10:34,233
Oh!

152
00:10:34,233 --> 00:10:36,080
Here they come. Smile.

153
00:10:43,713 --> 00:10:46,525
Chairman Cheon says
he has no appointment today.

154
00:10:46,525 --> 00:10:51,129
Oh, really? That's strange.

155
00:10:52,173 --> 00:10:53,369
He must've forgotten.

156
00:10:53,369 --> 00:10:57,080
Instead of standing here,
perhaps I should speak to him in person...

157
00:10:58,073 --> 00:11:02,013
He's already gone to his room to rest,
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

158
00:11:02,969 --> 00:11:04,849
He went in already.

159
00:11:08,725 --> 00:11:12,053
Escort these people downstairs
and tell the gate.

160
00:11:12,053 --> 00:11:16,341
If this happens one more time,
every one of them is getting fired.

161
00:11:16,341 --> 00:11:18,333
Yes, sir.

162
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:20,313
Please come with me.

163
00:11:26,297 --> 00:11:27,878
The view is incredible.

164
00:11:27,878 --> 00:11:30,737
It's so wide open. What a view.

165
00:11:30,737 --> 00:11:32,781
The wine's good, right?

166
00:11:32,781 --> 00:11:35,133
Huh? I've got some drinks.

167
00:11:35,133 --> 00:11:38,641
Not that cheap stuff. Drink something good.

168
00:11:38,641 --> 00:11:40,969
But you're unique and interesting.

169
00:11:40,969 --> 00:11:43,341
Honestly, you're not my type,

170
00:11:43,341 --> 00:11:45,380
but there's something kind of sexy about you.

171
00:11:48,313 --> 00:11:51,129
If you're here to play,
just play the darn game.

172
00:11:51,129 --> 00:11:53,269
Don't push your luck when you
haven't even been dealt a hand.

173
00:11:53,269 --> 00:11:55,397
Oh?

174
00:11:55,397 --> 00:11:57,946
I suddenly feel like
having something greasy, huh?

175
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:02,380
I can order room service, right?

176
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:04,764
Order whatever you want.

177
00:12:04,764 --> 00:12:06,613
And strong liquor...

178
00:12:07,577 --> 00:12:10,213
calls for greasy food.

179
00:12:14,117 --> 00:12:17,833
Tak Jong Gu just drugged the drink.
Just in case...

180
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:20,297
<i>No, it's too dangerous for you
to meet him there yourself.</i>

181
00:12:20,297 --> 00:12:22,885
That woman could become a witness,
and we don't even have an escape route yet...

182
00:12:22,885 --> 00:12:24,397
<i>Calm down, Ki Yeong Do.</i>

183
00:12:24,397 --> 00:12:26,933
Who's saying I'm meeting him right now?

184
00:12:26,933 --> 00:12:29,806
I'm just saying we need to prevent
anyone from getting hurt.

185
00:12:29,806 --> 00:12:31,417
<i>Well...</i>

186
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:34,246
Maybe just a punch in the face or something?

187
00:12:47,269 --> 00:12:50,845
For their sake, I hope you won't do
anything reckless again.

188
00:12:50,845 --> 00:12:55,813
Of course. What have these people done wrong?
Someone else is guilty.

189
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,846
Then please head back safely.

190
00:13:02,976 --> 00:13:05,846
That young man is almost annoyingly polite.

191
00:13:06,849 --> 00:13:11,946
Oh, we went all the way up there,
only to get kicked out empty-handed.

192
00:13:14,369 --> 00:13:16,401
Not empty-handed.

193
00:13:16,401 --> 00:13:18,157
- What?
- First.

194
00:13:18,157 --> 00:13:20,689
Chairman Cheon is
in the VIP gambling room now.

195
00:13:20,689 --> 00:13:22,941
Which means he was gambling.

196
00:13:22,941 --> 00:13:25,857
Chairman Cheon says
he has no appointments today.

197
00:13:25,857 --> 00:13:27,913
Oh, that's right.

198
00:13:27,913 --> 00:13:32,113
He didn't say there was no such person.
He said there was no appointment.

199
00:13:32,113 --> 00:13:34,905
Second, he's in his room right now.

200
00:13:34,905 --> 00:13:38,113
You're not seriously
going to his room, are you?

201
00:13:40,490 --> 00:13:43,813
Wait. Someone else is coming down the hall.

202
00:13:47,254 --> 00:13:48,954
Come in.

203
00:13:54,545 --> 00:13:56,646
What did she order?

204
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:05,125
Good!

205
00:14:19,273 --> 00:14:22,446
She said she was just washing her hands.
What's taking her so long?

206
00:14:37,353 --> 00:14:39,446
That worked fast, huh?

207
00:14:40,513 --> 00:14:42,537
<i>♪ If you don't come out, I'm busting in ♪</i>

208
00:14:42,537 --> 00:14:44,537
<i>♪ Dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>

209
00:14:44,537 --> 00:14:46,713
<i>♪ If you don't come out, I'm busting in ♪</i>

210
00:14:50,669 --> 00:14:53,039
Oh, dear.

211
00:14:53,039 --> 00:14:57,361
Our Jong Gu, Jong Gu, Mr. Tak Jong Gu.

212
00:14:57,361 --> 00:15:00,289
You're not the only one who can use drugs.

213
00:15:00,289 --> 00:15:03,846
He probably never imagined
he'd be the one on the receiving end.

214
00:15:13,301 --> 00:15:14,785
Yeong Do, something's wrong.

215
00:15:14,785 --> 00:15:17,164
<i>What is it? Is it the victim?</i>

216
00:15:17,164 --> 00:15:19,793
No, I think Tak Jong Gu was drugged.

217
00:15:19,793 --> 00:15:21,314
What?

218
00:15:21,314 --> 00:15:23,046
What do you mean...

219
00:15:25,677 --> 00:15:28,288
So, should I tell the boss to start?

220
00:15:28,288 --> 00:15:31,733
Not yet. There's something
we need to check first.

221
00:15:31,733 --> 00:15:33,713
There's...

222
00:15:34,617 --> 00:15:36,317
someone in the bathroom.

223
00:15:59,805 --> 00:16:00,805
Who are you?

224
00:16:00,805 --> 00:16:03,330
That's not a kitchen knife.

225
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:05,030
Are you a hitman?

226
00:16:23,885 --> 00:16:25,717
Yeah, this one's for people.

227
00:16:25,717 --> 00:16:26,989
We should at least
introduce ourselves, shouldn't we?

228
00:16:26,989 --> 00:16:28,345
- Do we have to?
- <i>Ms. Yoo, what's going on?</i>

229
00:16:28,345 --> 00:16:31,228
<i>What's happening? Ms. Yoo!</i>

230
00:16:32,541 --> 00:16:34,380
If you don't want to, we can skip it.

231
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:37,046
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo!

232
00:16:46,988 --> 00:16:49,317
Stay calm. Take it slow.

233
00:16:49,317 --> 00:16:50,673
Did she sound like a professional?

234
00:16:50,673 --> 00:16:53,717
Judging by the fact that
she's going up against Ms. Bo Na,

235
00:16:53,717 --> 00:16:56,385
she doesn't seem like an ordinary person.

236
00:16:56,385 --> 00:16:59,467
I'll go check out the situation first.

237
00:16:59,467 --> 00:17:01,413
Ms. Yoo's in too much danger.

238
00:17:04,001 --> 00:17:08,080
This is all my fault. I missed my pass.

239
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,781
<i>Calm down.</i>

240
00:17:09,781 --> 00:17:12,381
Director Yoo will be fine.

241
00:17:12,381 --> 00:17:13,788
This won't do.

242
00:17:13,788 --> 00:17:15,869
I'll take out all the CCTV cameras
in the building.

243
00:17:15,869 --> 00:17:20,046
Then the guards will all head
to the gaming room first.

244
00:17:30,752 --> 00:17:33,097
All the CCTV cameras just went down.

245
00:17:33,097 --> 00:17:35,485
Perfect timing. Let's start now.

246
00:17:35,485 --> 00:17:36,866
<i>Stand by.</i>

247
00:17:36,866 --> 00:17:38,946
Something just came up over here.

248
00:17:42,130 --> 00:17:44,480
What is taking so long?

249
00:17:47,781 --> 00:17:50,013
You lost?

250
00:18:10,645 --> 00:18:13,546
Looks like there aren't
any security guards here.

251
00:18:14,305 --> 00:18:16,437
That can't be.

252
00:18:16,437 --> 00:18:18,313
Could it be shift change?

253
00:18:58,941 --> 00:19:00,753
Huh?

254
00:19:00,753 --> 00:19:04,113
Didn't someone just walk past over there?

255
00:19:08,561 --> 00:19:09,980
What are you doing? Let go!

256
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:12,713
Shh. Just be quiet for a second.

257
00:19:15,701 --> 00:19:18,521
Let's quickly find
Chairman Cheon's room first.

258
00:19:18,521 --> 00:19:20,393
Oh, alright.

259
00:19:20,393 --> 00:19:23,546
You said it was the best room
on the 24th floor, right?

260
00:19:24,549 --> 00:19:26,713
Darn it, let go of this!

261
00:19:40,473 --> 00:19:42,173
Shh!

262
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:05,173
I'm in front of Tak Jong Gu's room.
It's quiet for now.

263
00:20:05,173 --> 00:20:06,980
But I'll go in.

264
00:20:26,813 --> 00:20:31,846
<i>♪ In those four beats, there is love ♪</i>

265
00:20:33,853 --> 00:20:35,713
There's a man too?

266
00:20:45,389 --> 00:20:48,646
He's just passed out from drinking.

267
00:20:49,481 --> 00:20:51,746
And who might you be?

268
00:20:57,221 --> 00:21:00,080
"Death conquers all evil."

269
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:02,080
That's what our boss always says.

270
00:21:04,369 --> 00:21:07,817
So you guys are behind
what happened to my face?

271
00:21:07,817 --> 00:21:11,180
It's only temporary.
The symptoms will subside with time.

272
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:14,046
You're the local team, aren't you?

273
00:21:16,289 --> 00:21:19,479
Well, things just got interesting.

274
00:21:19,479 --> 00:21:21,580
Are you guys Team A?

275
00:21:24,601 --> 00:21:27,061
It seems our clients have overlapped.

276
00:21:27,061 --> 00:21:29,280
That's never happened before.

277
00:21:30,529 --> 00:21:33,113
This should help ease the symptoms.

278
00:21:35,457 --> 00:21:37,881
But "overlap"?

279
00:21:37,881 --> 00:21:40,013
What do you mean?

280
00:21:40,825 --> 00:21:44,646
Isn't Tak Jong Gu your target?

281
00:21:47,985 --> 00:21:50,477
That punk was your target?

282
00:21:50,477 --> 00:21:52,753
No wonder.

283
00:21:52,753 --> 00:21:54,869
He wasn't ours.

284
00:21:54,869 --> 00:21:58,280
- Then...
- Our target is...

285
00:22:00,346 --> 00:22:02,780
Room 2408.

286
00:22:03,689 --> 00:22:05,480
- <i>♪ Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>
- <i>Gaecheon Construction,</i>

287
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:09,477
- <i>♪ In those four beats ♪</i>
- <i>Chairman Cheon Seong Gil.</i>

288
00:22:09,477 --> 00:22:14,413
<i>♪ There is love, and there are tears ♪</i>

289
00:22:20,549 --> 00:22:22,480
2408.

290
00:22:26,581 --> 00:22:29,180
Well, what a stroke of luck, huh?

291
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:31,513
You've just made my job easier.

292
00:22:32,529 --> 00:22:35,538
Hey, you, just leave.

293
00:22:35,538 --> 00:22:39,546
I'm letting you live as a special favor
for bringing me here.

294
00:22:40,849 --> 00:22:43,317
- What are you doing?
- Jeez.

295
00:22:43,317 --> 00:22:47,246
That's none of your business,
so leave while I'm letting you walk out.

296
00:22:47,246 --> 00:22:48,781
You don't exactly look

297
00:22:48,781 --> 00:22:52,446
innocent enough to go around
calling yourself a witness,

298
00:22:52,446 --> 00:22:55,041
so I'm letting you go.

299
00:22:55,041 --> 00:22:57,429
I only want to kill one person today.

300
00:22:57,429 --> 00:22:59,129
- Hey!
- Darn it!

301
00:23:03,861 --> 00:23:07,165
Ms. Yoo, can you hear me? Ms. Yoo?

302
00:23:07,165 --> 00:23:09,297
Please, say something! Please!

303
00:23:09,297 --> 00:23:10,441
Ms. Yoo!

304
00:23:10,441 --> 00:23:13,846
I need to know why you're trying to kill him.

305
00:23:18,121 --> 00:23:19,585
I gave you a fair chance.

306
00:23:19,585 --> 00:23:20,969
I gave you one too.

307
00:23:20,969 --> 00:23:22,234
Are you a hired killer?

308
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:23,917
She is with the local team.

309
00:23:23,917 --> 00:23:25,273
Are you listening?

310
00:23:25,273 --> 00:23:28,180
Ms. Yoo, you have to stop, please!

311
00:23:32,033 --> 00:23:34,013
I'm not holding back anymore.

312
00:23:34,013 --> 00:23:35,013
Fine. Go ahead.

313
00:23:35,013 --> 00:23:36,546
Ms. Yoo!

314
00:23:36,546 --> 00:23:38,546
Ms. Yoo, please...

315
00:23:48,161 --> 00:23:51,793
<i>♪ Dun-da, Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>

316
00:23:51,793 --> 00:23:55,513
<i>♪ In those four beats ♪</i>

317
00:23:55,513 --> 00:23:59,246
<i>♪ There is love, and there are tears ♪</i>

318
00:23:59,246 --> 00:24:03,181
<i>♪ And there is farewell too ♪</i>

319
00:24:03,181 --> 00:24:05,773
<i>♪ With each verse, each hurdle ♪</i>

320
00:24:05,773 --> 00:24:08,746
<i>♪ When you overcome it ♪</i>

321
00:24:20,265 --> 00:24:22,549
I think this is it, right?

322
00:24:22,549 --> 00:24:26,113
But don't you hear something inside?

323
00:24:52,265 --> 00:24:54,537
Sounds like some guys
horsing around in there.

324
00:24:54,537 --> 00:24:56,813
Isn't this the place?

325
00:24:59,529 --> 00:25:01,761
What's going on?

326
00:25:01,761 --> 00:25:04,489
Do you need any help?

327
00:25:04,489 --> 00:25:06,189
No.

328
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,737
I must've gotten the room wrong.

329
00:25:10,737 --> 00:25:12,401
I told you it wasn't this room, didn't I?

330
00:25:12,401 --> 00:25:14,412
See? I told you I was right.

331
00:25:14,412 --> 00:25:16,505
- It's upstairs.
- I said it's the floor above.

332
00:25:16,505 --> 00:25:19,469
I've been telling you this whole time.
It's the floor above.

333
00:25:19,469 --> 00:25:21,966
But this is the top floor, though.

334
00:25:21,966 --> 00:25:26,017
<i>Suspicious people are lurking in front of
room 2408, so go check it out.</i>

335
00:25:26,017 --> 00:25:28,213
Yeah, I'm going right now.

336
00:25:29,565 --> 00:25:32,449
Wow, we almost got caught.

337
00:25:32,449 --> 00:25:35,745
I thought my heart was going to explode.

338
00:25:35,745 --> 00:25:37,697
I think she's gone.

339
00:25:37,697 --> 00:25:40,349
I'm too scared to keep going.

340
00:25:40,349 --> 00:25:42,513
Can't we just pull out for today?

341
00:25:42,513 --> 00:25:44,697
Come on, what have you even done? Get up.

342
00:25:44,697 --> 00:25:48,246
Even if we're pulling out,
we should at least ring the doorbell first.

343
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:55,780
Wait, hold up!

344
00:25:57,753 --> 00:25:59,565
Please don't misunderstand
the current situation.

345
00:25:59,565 --> 00:26:00,780
The employees downstairs

346
00:26:00,780 --> 00:26:02,613
- are completely innocent.
- Shh!

347
00:26:05,025 --> 00:26:08,249
Don't do anything else.
Just go straight down to the first floor.

348
00:26:08,249 --> 00:26:11,580
If you leave the building now,
I'll pretend I never saw you.

349
00:26:17,613 --> 00:26:19,313
What was that?

350
00:26:21,541 --> 00:26:23,127
Darn it!

351
00:26:23,127 --> 00:26:24,980
Seriously...

352
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:32,101
You're good at scurrying away like a rat.

353
00:26:32,101 --> 00:26:35,495
How long are you going to keep blocking me?

354
00:26:35,495 --> 00:26:39,646
Oh... Is blocking all you can do?

355
00:26:40,353 --> 00:26:41,627
Curious?

356
00:26:41,627 --> 00:26:43,327
You!

357
00:26:54,233 --> 00:26:56,580
Then try blocking me yourself.

358
00:27:12,969 --> 00:27:16,480
What are you? What kind of woman are you?

359
00:27:18,425 --> 00:27:20,280
The water stopped.

360
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:29,880
Director Yoo Bo Na, it's me!

361
00:27:30,641 --> 00:27:32,341
You...

362
00:27:38,765 --> 00:27:42,973
<i>♪ Dun-da, Dun-da, dun-da-dun-da-dun ♪</i>

363
00:27:42,973 --> 00:27:46,513
<i>♪ In those four beats ♪</i>

364
00:27:53,401 --> 00:27:55,397
Oh, yeah, Secretary Kim.

365
00:27:55,397 --> 00:27:58,797
After that soak, I'm getting a little hungry.

366
00:27:58,797 --> 00:28:01,680
Shall I grab a bite before heading down?

367
00:28:02,332 --> 00:28:04,661
Alright, alright.

368
00:28:04,661 --> 00:28:09,537
<i>♪ There is love, and there is farewell ♪</i>

369
00:28:09,537 --> 00:28:13,380
<i>♪ And there are tears too ♪</i>

370
00:28:16,546 --> 00:28:20,246
What a spectacular day this has been.

371
00:28:20,246 --> 00:28:22,333
How are your nerves holding up?

372
00:28:22,333 --> 00:28:24,921
You're scared out of your wits.

373
00:28:24,921 --> 00:28:28,813
I didn't know meeting one person
could be this hard.

374
00:28:33,701 --> 00:28:36,313
It's like a giant fortress.

375
00:28:37,173 --> 00:28:39,646
Like a solid castle wall.

376
00:28:39,646 --> 00:28:41,213
It does.

377
00:28:41,213 --> 00:28:45,002
In movies, places that look this glamorous

378
00:28:45,002 --> 00:28:48,546
usually have some dark secret
lurking underneath.

379
00:28:49,309 --> 00:28:53,013
Eventually, those secrets
always come to light.

380
00:28:54,080 --> 00:28:57,046
That's what people like us are here for.

381
00:28:59,222 --> 00:29:00,222
Nice to meet you.

382
00:29:00,222 --> 00:29:02,523
I'm Bae Bi Ji, owner of Dalsam Auto.

383
00:29:02,547 --> 00:29:07,243
Hello. I'm Go Yeong Gap, Manager of
Sales Team 3 at Durumi Electronics.

384
00:29:07,243 --> 00:29:12,167
Oh, and this is our team hacker,
Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do.

385
00:29:12,167 --> 00:29:14,458
A hacker?

386
00:29:14,458 --> 00:29:17,952
So the CCTV going down was his doing.

387
00:29:17,952 --> 00:29:22,043
I've heard there are separate teams
for different regions and assignments,

388
00:29:22,043 --> 00:29:23,643
but this is my first time
meeting you in person.

389
00:29:23,643 --> 00:29:25,051
Well, unless something unexpected
like this happens,

390
00:29:25,051 --> 00:29:27,224
we don't really cross paths.

391
00:29:28,199 --> 00:29:29,355
Oh, and this is...

392
00:29:29,355 --> 00:29:31,865
Oh, no need to introduce her.
I know her well.

393
00:29:31,865 --> 00:29:35,724
Is there anyone in this line of work
who doesn't know Director Yoo?

394
00:29:36,391 --> 00:29:38,375
I've met her before too.

395
00:29:38,375 --> 00:29:40,224
Back when Ms. Bae was team leader.

396
00:29:41,093 --> 00:29:42,427
Yeah.

397
00:29:42,427 --> 00:29:45,424
You were just a rookie back then.
You're a team leader already?

398
00:29:46,083 --> 00:29:49,624
Well, it wasn't exactly intentional.
There's a bit of a story behind it.

399
00:29:50,279 --> 00:29:52,015
Oh, these are our employees.

400
00:29:52,015 --> 00:29:54,403
This is Ms. Mun Meo Ru,
who mainly works in the field.

401
00:29:54,403 --> 00:29:58,207
Wow, it's a miracle she survived
going up against you, Director Yoo.

402
00:29:58,207 --> 00:30:00,217
Didn't you go a little easy on her?

403
00:30:00,217 --> 00:30:01,489
What? She was pretty good.

404
00:30:01,489 --> 00:30:04,643
Though she does seem a little reckless.

405
00:30:04,643 --> 00:30:08,924
Yes, well, thank you for sparing me.

406
00:30:12,571 --> 00:30:17,223
And this is our team's idea machine,
our part-timer, Ms. Mun Da Rae.

407
00:30:17,223 --> 00:30:19,939
Oh, it's cold.

408
00:30:19,939 --> 00:30:23,491
She seems to have the most experience,
but her position is still just part-time.

409
00:30:23,491 --> 00:30:26,899
She really hates being
responsible for anything.

410
00:30:26,899 --> 00:30:28,287
You know me, right?

411
00:30:28,287 --> 00:30:29,752
We met at the casino earlier.

412
00:30:29,752 --> 00:30:32,791
I know you, chicken heart.

413
00:30:33,830 --> 00:30:35,531
But how did you pull that off?

414
00:30:35,531 --> 00:30:39,287
You had a higher win rate
than the program I designed.

415
00:30:39,287 --> 00:30:41,555
Use your brain, your brain.

416
00:30:41,555 --> 00:30:45,706
You stupidly cling to machines,
so you get outsmarted that stupidly.

417
00:30:45,706 --> 00:30:47,691
Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

418
00:30:48,827 --> 00:30:52,591
Our part-timer is brilliant,
but she's a little lacking in social skills.

419
00:30:55,327 --> 00:30:58,032
Then shall we hear about your client?

420
00:30:58,032 --> 00:31:01,158
Oh, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil?

421
00:31:01,831 --> 00:31:04,451
In a nutshell, he's a serial sexual predator.

422
00:31:04,451 --> 00:31:06,355
He was caught red-handed a few years ago,

423
00:31:06,355 --> 00:31:08,779
but got away with a suspended sentence.

424
00:31:08,779 --> 00:31:13,159
<i>He hired the wife of one of his
construction workers as a housekeeper,</i>

425
00:31:13,159 --> 00:31:16,847
<i>and repeatedly sexually assaulted her
by threatening her husband's job.</i>

426
00:31:16,847 --> 00:31:18,315
Her husband found out

427
00:31:18,315 --> 00:31:22,191
and threatened to go to the press
unless he confessed.

428
00:31:22,191 --> 00:31:26,143
<i>So, Chairman Cheon bribed
a fellow worker with a criminal record</i>

429
00:31:26,143 --> 00:31:28,003
<i>and had him murder the husband.</i>

430
00:31:28,003 --> 00:31:29,771
<i>Then he covered it up by staging the murder</i>

431
00:31:29,771 --> 00:31:33,419
<i>as an accidental fall caused by
the victim's own negligence.</i>

432
00:31:33,419 --> 00:31:35,991
Help me! Please!

433
00:31:35,991 --> 00:31:39,202
Save me! I was wrong.
I said I was wrong. Please save me.

434
00:31:39,202 --> 00:31:41,647
<i>We just met with the coworker</i>

435
00:31:41,647 --> 00:31:44,024
<i>who was hired
to kill the husband a few days ago.</i>

436
00:31:45,851 --> 00:31:51,024
Chairman Cheon must be thrilled that
the guy who had dirt on him is dead.

437
00:31:52,891 --> 00:31:53,891
Oh, right!

438
00:31:53,891 --> 00:31:58,046
I think two reporters were following
Chairman Cheon earlier.

439
00:31:58,046 --> 00:31:59,160
Reporters?

440
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:01,579
The media lost interest quickly

441
00:32:01,579 --> 00:32:03,675
because Chairman Cheon
cleverly covered up the case.

442
00:32:03,675 --> 00:32:08,155
So I thought it was interesting that
reporters are still digging into it.

443
00:32:08,155 --> 00:32:10,424
They seemed pretty persistent.

444
00:32:10,424 --> 00:32:14,451
I sent them away because it seemed dangerous
if they kept getting closer,

445
00:32:14,451 --> 00:32:16,324
but I'm not sure if they've actually left.

446
00:32:20,391 --> 00:32:22,224
Yul, I'll close the door. Watch your hand.

447
00:32:23,927 --> 00:32:26,543
But, honey, are you
really sure you have time?

448
00:32:26,543 --> 00:32:29,587
If you think it might be tough,
should we quickly ask Se Ah now?

449
00:32:29,587 --> 00:32:33,251
I do have an interview
a little farther away...

450
00:32:33,251 --> 00:32:34,727
But I should be fine. I can make it on time.

451
00:32:34,727 --> 00:32:37,167
Bad guys don't usually give you much time.

452
00:32:37,167 --> 00:32:38,647
Yeah? A bad guy?

453
00:32:38,647 --> 00:32:40,624
How bad is this guy?

454
00:32:41,710 --> 00:32:46,158
On the surface, it looks like an accident,
but a premeditated murder underneath?

455
00:32:46,158 --> 00:32:49,724
I'm going to expose the person
who ordered it and make sure he pays.

456
00:32:55,459 --> 00:32:57,607
So why did you go after Tak Jong Gu?

457
00:32:57,607 --> 00:33:01,459
We were looking for a fool
who could get us onto the VIP floor.

458
00:33:01,459 --> 00:33:05,352
We planned to set that room on fire
and sneak into Cheon Seong Gil's room

459
00:33:05,352 --> 00:33:07,358
during the chaos for the meeting.

460
00:33:08,067 --> 00:33:09,924
You came up with
quite a complicated scenario.

461
00:33:09,924 --> 00:33:15,232
Coming all the way to a casino,
and even playing games yourself to do it?

462
00:33:15,232 --> 00:33:19,591
She just made it fit
because she wanted to gamble.

463
00:33:21,999 --> 00:33:24,603
Anyway, they weren't even
particularly difficult meetings,

464
00:33:24,603 --> 00:33:26,935
but since our dates and routes overlapped,

465
00:33:26,935 --> 00:33:29,691
we ended up unintentionally
interfering with each other.

466
00:33:31,891 --> 00:33:36,791
Since we're already in this together,
how about we work together this time?

467
00:33:38,231 --> 00:33:40,558
Well, sounds like a good idea.

468
00:33:40,558 --> 00:33:44,258
- I'm in.
- If Ms. Yoo is okay with it, I'm fine too.

469
00:33:45,271 --> 00:33:51,259
We've never worked together before,
so we don't know each other's styles.

470
00:33:51,259 --> 00:33:52,931
Isn't this a bit of a gamble?

471
00:33:52,931 --> 00:33:55,415
Oh, I like a gamble.

472
00:33:55,415 --> 00:33:57,071
- I'm in!
- I'm against it.

473
00:33:57,071 --> 00:33:58,475
I'm not feeling great.

474
00:33:58,475 --> 00:34:00,419
Well, looks like the vote went in favor.

475
00:34:00,419 --> 00:34:01,843
Let's do the collaboration.

476
00:34:01,843 --> 00:34:05,091
Jeez, she always does whatever she wants.

477
00:34:07,858 --> 00:34:09,899
Yeah, we should.

478
00:34:09,899 --> 00:34:12,958
Our part-timer is a bit of a dictator.

479
00:34:14,579 --> 00:34:17,043
But we have to wrap up the meeting
by tomorrow.

480
00:34:17,043 --> 00:34:19,935
Do we have time to rework the scenario?

481
00:34:19,935 --> 00:34:21,124
Why drag it out till tomorrow?

482
00:34:21,124 --> 00:34:23,491
We've already got the whole story.

483
00:34:23,491 --> 00:34:25,943
For this one...

484
00:34:25,943 --> 00:34:28,036
let's go with Go-Stop.

485
00:34:28,036 --> 00:34:31,691
Kill two birds with one stone.

486
00:34:31,691 --> 00:34:35,651
<i>Isn't it risky to meet Tak Jong Gu again?</i>

487
00:34:35,651 --> 00:34:37,458
<i>If he finds out we drugged him...</i>

488
00:34:38,931 --> 00:34:40,223
All mine!

489
00:34:40,223 --> 00:34:41,771
<i>He's a junkie.</i>

490
00:34:41,771 --> 00:34:43,363
<i>He'll think the wine was switched by mistake</i>

491
00:34:43,363 --> 00:34:45,575
<i>and that he drank his own drugged wine.</i>

492
00:34:45,575 --> 00:34:46,702
What?

493
00:34:46,702 --> 00:34:48,075
I thought you'd left. You're still here?

494
00:34:48,075 --> 00:34:50,026
I got a room too.

495
00:34:50,026 --> 00:34:51,991
Are you sober now?

496
00:34:51,991 --> 00:34:53,399
Yeah.

497
00:34:53,399 --> 00:34:59,391
Well, I'm usually a heavy drinker,
but one lousy drink knocked me out.

498
00:35:00,095 --> 00:35:02,658
Anyway, good to see you again.

499
00:35:02,658 --> 00:35:05,058
Oh, this is boring.

500
00:35:05,058 --> 00:35:07,151
Why is there no thrill in this?

501
00:35:07,151 --> 00:35:10,224
I'm not feeling any dopamine.

502
00:35:11,787 --> 00:35:14,179
Want to come back to my room?

503
00:35:14,179 --> 00:35:16,723
I've got something seriously killer.

504
00:35:16,723 --> 00:35:21,567
You pathetic junkie prick who thinks
your rich dad makes you untouchable.

505
00:35:21,567 --> 00:35:22,567
What?

506
00:35:22,567 --> 00:35:24,999
Someone said that about you.

507
00:35:24,999 --> 00:35:26,199
Is that true?

508
00:35:26,199 --> 00:35:28,011
Who said that?

509
00:35:28,011 --> 00:35:30,695
Which punk talked nonsense like that?

510
00:35:30,695 --> 00:35:32,916
Over there...

511
00:35:32,916 --> 00:35:35,091
some old guy with a big belly.

512
00:35:36,215 --> 00:35:38,103
Your name is Tak Jong Gu, right?

513
00:35:38,103 --> 00:35:39,995
I heard he's some chairman.

514
00:35:39,995 --> 00:35:43,363
Oh, Gaecheon Construction?

515
00:35:43,363 --> 00:35:44,935
Gaecheon?

516
00:35:44,935 --> 00:35:46,747
Has the old man lost his mind?

517
00:35:46,747 --> 00:35:48,491
Give me a good hand.

518
00:35:51,851 --> 00:35:54,044
Oh, my, what is this?

519
00:35:54,044 --> 00:35:57,091
- Old man, have you lost your mind?
- Oh, my, what's this?

520
00:35:57,091 --> 00:36:00,743
You little punk who keeps paying off
my old man every quarter.

521
00:36:00,743 --> 00:36:02,813
You think you're untouchable, huh?

522
00:36:02,813 --> 00:36:04,124
Hey, what are you? Hey!

523
00:36:04,124 --> 00:36:06,323
- What on earth are you...
- Watch your mouth, or else, huh?

524
00:36:06,323 --> 00:36:08,743
Maybe you'll come to your senses
when your company goes under.

525
00:36:08,743 --> 00:36:10,151
Darn it!

526
00:36:10,151 --> 00:36:11,851
Hey!

527
00:36:14,027 --> 00:36:18,239
- What are you?
- <i>That should be enough witnesses.</i>

528
00:36:18,239 --> 00:36:21,051
- <i>What's next?</i>
- Wow...

529
00:36:21,051 --> 00:36:24,791
I really like that
you're a total punk, Jong Gu.

530
00:36:27,259 --> 00:36:29,724
That killer stuff you mentioned earlier...

531
00:36:30,483 --> 00:36:32,224
is that offer still good?

532
00:36:35,335 --> 00:36:37,035
Are you interested in that?

533
00:36:37,651 --> 00:36:39,391
Of course, it is.

534
00:36:40,479 --> 00:36:43,324
One dose, and you're off to heaven.

535
00:36:45,927 --> 00:36:48,255
Bring that to my room in an hour.

536
00:36:48,255 --> 00:36:50,824
Without anyone knowing.

537
00:36:56,343 --> 00:37:02,047
When Tak Jong Gu walks into the room
and finds Chairman Cheon dead,

538
00:37:02,047 --> 00:37:04,358
he'll be shocked into passing out.

539
00:37:04,358 --> 00:37:09,711
Yeah, we'll give the unconscious guy
the drug we brought first.

540
00:37:09,711 --> 00:37:14,107
Then Team A can go in
and finish off Tak Jong Gu.

541
00:37:14,107 --> 00:37:15,467
Bingo!

542
00:37:15,467 --> 00:37:20,137
Tak Jong Gu, still furious even after
causing that scene in the gaming room,

543
00:37:20,137 --> 00:37:22,827
takes a full dose of drugs, loses his mind,

544
00:37:22,827 --> 00:37:25,015
and storms into Cheon Seong Gil's room.

545
00:37:25,015 --> 00:37:26,924
We'll take him out first.

546
00:37:26,924 --> 00:37:32,151
Then he'll throw himself
out the window. Boom!

547
00:37:32,151 --> 00:37:33,851
Done.

548
00:37:45,340 --> 00:37:46,767
[Big Precious]

549
00:37:49,791 --> 00:37:52,624
Honey, I'm on my way to pick up Yul.
I'm almost there.

550
00:37:52,624 --> 00:37:54,322
Are you going to Seo Yeon's place now?

551
00:37:54,322 --> 00:37:55,995
I'm sorry, I'm a bit late, right?

552
00:37:55,995 --> 00:37:59,083
But I called ahead to let them know.

553
00:37:59,083 --> 00:38:00,981
No, I'm not nagging you.

554
00:38:00,981 --> 00:38:02,655
<i>Have you eaten?</i>

555
00:38:02,655 --> 00:38:05,831
I can just eat at home later.
What about you, honey?

556
00:38:05,831 --> 00:38:08,463
Well, I grabbed something quick.

557
00:38:08,463 --> 00:38:11,267
I'm still out. I haven't finished work yet.

558
00:38:11,267 --> 00:38:12,783
Still?

559
00:38:12,783 --> 00:38:15,979
Didn't you have a client meeting today?
Did it not go well?

560
00:38:15,979 --> 00:38:20,591
Oh, the meeting fell through this afternoon,
so it got pushed to tonight.

561
00:38:21,531 --> 00:38:24,395
Did the interview with the bad guy go well?

562
00:38:24,395 --> 00:38:26,055
<i>Me? Well...</i>

563
00:38:26,055 --> 00:38:28,179
It's not like I had an appointment with him.

564
00:38:28,179 --> 00:38:32,575
And bad guys don't usually
give interviews willingly, you know.

565
00:38:32,575 --> 00:38:33,575
<i>Then what do I do?</i>

566
00:38:33,575 --> 00:38:35,243
I just have to barge in.

567
00:38:35,243 --> 00:38:36,867
So, did you meet him?

568
00:38:36,867 --> 00:38:40,959
I did meet him,
but I got kicked out right away.

569
00:38:40,959 --> 00:38:43,223
I couldn't even ask one question.

570
00:38:43,223 --> 00:38:44,959
Oh, I see.

571
00:38:44,959 --> 00:38:48,159
It's okay. I'll just barge in again tomorrow.

572
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:49,819
Honey, I'm almost there.

573
00:38:49,819 --> 00:38:51,191
<i>Can we talk again later?</i>

574
00:38:51,191 --> 00:38:52,224
Yul's probably waiting.

575
00:38:52,224 --> 00:38:53,324
<i>Yeah, okay.</i>

576
00:38:53,324 --> 00:38:54,899
Make sure you eat.

577
00:38:54,899 --> 00:38:56,599
<i>Okay.</i>

578
00:39:08,835 --> 00:39:12,624
Tak Jong Gu's actions are not deviating
from expectations one bit.

579
00:39:12,624 --> 00:39:15,691
Everything went according to plan
up to the gaming room.

580
00:39:16,387 --> 00:39:18,087
Yeah.

581
00:39:19,463 --> 00:39:21,783
You've seemed a little off, Ms. Yoo.

582
00:39:21,783 --> 00:39:24,491
Is something bothering you?

583
00:39:27,464 --> 00:39:30,105
I saw my husband at the casino earlier.

584
00:39:30,105 --> 00:39:31,805
Your husband?

585
00:39:34,055 --> 00:39:37,191
<i>Then that man I saw earlier was...</i>

586
00:39:37,191 --> 00:39:39,039
I'll find out where he is right now.

587
00:39:39,039 --> 00:39:40,585
I just talked to him on the phone.

588
00:39:40,585 --> 00:39:42,139
He said he's on his way home.

589
00:39:42,139 --> 00:39:44,491
We won't run into each other anymore.

590
00:39:46,023 --> 00:39:49,424
But your husband being here...

591
00:39:50,671 --> 00:39:52,624
Could it be that gambling...

592
00:39:53,739 --> 00:39:55,524
That can't be right.

593
00:39:56,315 --> 00:39:58,123
Sorry.

594
00:39:58,123 --> 00:40:01,451
He said he had an interview
out of town today.

595
00:40:01,451 --> 00:40:03,787
But I didn't expect him to be here.

596
00:40:03,787 --> 00:40:06,224
An interview, with whom?

597
00:40:06,224 --> 00:40:09,891
Oh, the reporter who's digging into
Chairman Cheon...

598
00:40:12,711 --> 00:40:14,287
Let's get to work.

599
00:40:14,287 --> 00:40:17,084
Where are the two of them now?

600
00:40:17,084 --> 00:40:21,259
Okay, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
just went into his room,

601
00:40:21,259 --> 00:40:24,379
and Tak Jong Gu went into his room too.

602
00:40:24,379 --> 00:40:26,307
Then the timing should work.

603
00:40:26,307 --> 00:40:28,524
Okay, shall we go?

604
00:40:30,083 --> 00:40:31,783
Ms. Yoo.

605
00:40:33,239 --> 00:40:35,531
Never leave me out again.

606
00:40:35,531 --> 00:40:38,143
That won't happen again, okay?

607
00:40:38,143 --> 00:40:39,843
I'm going.

608
00:41:07,739 --> 00:41:09,199
Wow!

609
00:41:09,199 --> 00:41:10,899
Nice room!

610
00:41:14,379 --> 00:41:17,873
My baby, where are you?

611
00:41:17,873 --> 00:41:20,283
Are you getting ready for something special?

612
00:41:20,283 --> 00:41:22,558
I love the outfit you had on earlier.

613
00:41:33,199 --> 00:41:36,707
That darn punk made me shower again.

614
00:41:36,707 --> 00:41:39,155
I'm so annoyed.

615
00:41:39,155 --> 00:41:41,624
Oh, my, so annoying.

616
00:41:43,263 --> 00:41:44,919
What? Who are you?

617
00:41:44,919 --> 00:41:47,158
Who are you? Huh?

618
00:41:50,471 --> 00:41:53,623
You little punk, you...

619
00:41:53,623 --> 00:41:56,267
Why on earth are you here?

620
00:41:56,267 --> 00:41:58,351
What are you doing in my woman's room?

621
00:41:58,351 --> 00:42:01,991
Jeez, you punk, you're in for it now.

622
00:42:01,991 --> 00:42:06,399
Get over here! You punk!

623
00:42:06,399 --> 00:42:07,891
Punk?

624
00:42:07,891 --> 00:42:10,324
Should I tear you apart?

625
00:42:22,983 --> 00:42:24,371
You two make quite a pair.

626
00:42:24,371 --> 00:42:26,991
I think there's a simpler way,
don't you think?

627
00:42:26,991 --> 00:42:32,327
I saw a small light outside
Chairman Cheon's room window.

628
00:42:32,327 --> 00:42:36,687
You're good at scurrying away like a rat.

629
00:42:36,687 --> 00:42:39,058
How long are you going to keep blocking me?

630
00:42:40,158 --> 00:42:42,458
If I'm right...

631
00:42:46,311 --> 00:42:48,011
You're right.

632
00:42:49,224 --> 00:42:53,075
<i>Cheon Seong Gil's room and Tak Jong Gu's room
are on the opposite rear line.</i>

633
00:42:53,075 --> 00:42:55,191
<i>Outside those windows,
there are two mountains on either end,</i>

634
00:42:55,191 --> 00:42:59,459
<i>and a cable car is running
back and forth between them.</i>

635
00:42:59,459 --> 00:43:01,159
Then...

636
00:43:03,159 --> 00:43:07,115
As things stand, everyone here
could be called in by the police

637
00:43:07,115 --> 00:43:08,859
during the investigation.

638
00:43:08,859 --> 00:43:14,067
Especially those who had direct contact
with Cheon Seong Gil and Tak Jong Gu.

639
00:43:14,067 --> 00:43:15,763
There'll be plenty of witnesses.

640
00:43:15,763 --> 00:43:18,767
Let's just take the long way
and kill two birds with one stone, yeah?

641
00:43:18,767 --> 00:43:20,467
You're right.

642
00:43:25,358 --> 00:43:26,439
Hey, you punk!

643
00:43:26,439 --> 00:43:29,611
How dare some young punk
talk to an adult like that?

644
00:43:29,611 --> 00:43:33,427
Darn it! Hey! You want me
to chop your hand off?

645
00:43:33,427 --> 00:43:35,695
You ungrateful punk!

646
00:43:35,695 --> 00:43:37,223
I've been letting you get away with it,
but now you've gone too far!

647
00:43:37,223 --> 00:43:40,371
- Give it to me!
- Hand it over!

648
00:43:40,371 --> 00:43:42,847
I'll make you go through exactly
what I went through.

649
00:43:42,847 --> 00:43:44,151
Why won't this open?

650
00:43:44,151 --> 00:43:48,075
Hey, that's expensive, okay?

651
00:43:48,075 --> 00:43:49,324
Give that up, you old geezer!

652
00:43:49,324 --> 00:43:50,991
What?

653
00:43:50,991 --> 00:43:53,119
What? You little...

654
00:43:53,119 --> 00:43:55,499
What? Old geezer?

655
00:43:55,499 --> 00:43:57,783
Darn it!

656
00:43:57,783 --> 00:44:00,023
Old geezer! Old geezer!

657
00:44:00,023 --> 00:44:01,924
Okay, shall we go?

658
00:44:37,103 --> 00:44:39,091
Give it back! It's mine!

659
00:45:05,443 --> 00:45:08,258
One-two, client meeting completed.

660
00:45:24,579 --> 00:45:27,479
Alright, good work, everyone.

661
00:45:27,479 --> 00:45:30,459
Get some good rest tomorrow,
and I'll see you all the day after.

662
00:45:30,459 --> 00:45:32,159
Yeah.

663
00:45:37,391 --> 00:45:41,667
I wish I'd gotten to see
that historic moment with my own eyes.

664
00:45:41,667 --> 00:45:43,224
At least we saved the cost of a bullet.

665
00:45:43,224 --> 00:45:46,079
Our operating expenses were already tight.

666
00:45:46,079 --> 00:45:51,127
But I never knew there were people
in the area doing the same thing.

667
00:45:51,127 --> 00:45:55,924
There are too many bad guys in the world
for us to handle them all ourselves.

668
00:45:59,959 --> 00:46:01,924
Rest in peace, everyone.

669
00:46:03,079 --> 00:46:05,258
You two are headed the same way,

670
00:46:06,331 --> 00:46:08,491
so at least you won't be bored.

671
00:46:14,342 --> 00:46:17,391
Is our Tae Soon thirsty?

672
00:46:17,391 --> 00:46:21,695
Oh, alright. I'll give you some more water.

673
00:46:21,695 --> 00:46:26,023
Drink plenty of water,
and let's live together for a long time.

674
00:46:26,023 --> 00:46:29,524
I'll even get you another supplement
for your birthday this year.

675
00:46:32,369 --> 00:46:35,224
Looks like someone made Yoo Bo Na mad.

676
00:46:36,243 --> 00:46:39,324
No, it's nothing. Not you.
I mean, your owner.

677
00:46:39,324 --> 00:46:42,524
Yeah, want some more water?

678
00:46:42,524 --> 00:46:44,224
Yeah.

679
00:46:47,131 --> 00:46:49,324
Oh, my, so pretty!

680
00:46:49,324 --> 00:46:52,024
Alright, alright.

681
00:46:55,947 --> 00:46:58,443
Wow, as expected of Kingfisher.

682
00:46:58,443 --> 00:47:02,824
I finally got to meet the legend I've only
heard about. Today is my lucky day.

683
00:47:03,474 --> 00:47:04,474
You happy?

684
00:47:04,474 --> 00:47:08,223
What's so exciting about
getting carried by someone else?

685
00:47:08,223 --> 00:47:11,724
At least we won't
be getting called in by the police.

686
00:47:11,724 --> 00:47:14,724
There's no more perfect alibi than this.

687
00:47:15,711 --> 00:47:19,243
Hey, we're done for the day,
so let's go get some drinks.

688
00:47:19,243 --> 00:47:22,424
A day like this calls for chicken and beer.

689
00:47:23,855 --> 00:47:26,107
It's on me today.

690
00:47:26,107 --> 00:47:28,791
Ah, on me, on me!

691
00:47:29,563 --> 00:47:31,623
She looks the happiest of all.

692
00:47:31,623 --> 00:47:33,931
No, she's scared right now.

693
00:47:33,931 --> 00:47:37,679
She's just pretending to be tough.

694
00:47:37,679 --> 00:47:39,291
Hey, why don't you quit gambling
while you're at it?

695
00:47:39,291 --> 00:47:44,319
Hurry up! Whoever's late has to
write their name with their butt!

696
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:47,058
Da Rae, I'll just be late!

697
00:47:47,855 --> 00:47:49,247
Oh, how embarrassing.

698
00:47:49,247 --> 00:47:53,203
Oh, this is so humiliating. Oh, I hate this.

699
00:47:53,203 --> 00:47:55,291
Oh, being the boss is really hard.

700
00:47:55,291 --> 00:47:57,124
What's wrong with him?

701
00:48:00,359 --> 00:48:01,807
Daddy, why isn't Mommy here?

702
00:48:01,807 --> 00:48:04,577
I told you Mommy was staying the night.

703
00:48:04,577 --> 00:48:08,091
If Yul goes to sleep
and goes to daycare tomorrow,

704
00:48:08,091 --> 00:48:10,783
Mommy will be there to greet you with, "Yul!"

705
00:48:10,783 --> 00:48:12,735
But where did Mommy go?

706
00:48:12,735 --> 00:48:14,611
She went to work.

707
00:48:14,611 --> 00:48:16,355
Hmm... Something important?

708
00:48:16,355 --> 00:48:19,324
Huh? What kind of work?

709
00:48:20,798 --> 00:48:24,079
Wait, wait.

710
00:48:24,079 --> 00:48:26,824
Sit down here for a minute. Have a seat.

711
00:48:29,526 --> 00:48:31,719
Oh, Ms. Gu, did you get home okay?

712
00:48:31,719 --> 00:48:32,719
What made you call this late?

713
00:48:32,719 --> 00:48:36,471
Mr. Kwon, did you see the breaking news?

714
00:48:36,471 --> 00:48:38,011
Breaking news?

715
00:48:38,011 --> 00:48:40,311
What is it? But what's wrong with your voice?

716
00:48:40,311 --> 00:48:44,567
Chairman Cheon Seong Gil... is dead.
He was shot by Kingfisher.

717
00:48:44,567 --> 00:48:46,359
What?

718
00:48:46,359 --> 00:48:48,971
<i>Two guests were shot and killed</i>

719
00:48:48,971 --> 00:48:52,831
<i>by a sniper in a VIP suite
at a casino hotel this evening.</i>

720
00:48:52,831 --> 00:48:57,675
<i>Police are leaning toward Kingfisher
being behind this attack as well.</i>

721
00:48:57,675 --> 00:48:59,163
[Kingfisher Strikes Again]
<i>This is the first time</i>

722
00:48:59,163 --> 00:49:01,862
[Two Casino VIP Guests Killed]
<i>two people have been killed</i>

723
00:49:01,862 --> 00:49:03,171
<i>in a single Kingfisher case.</i>

724
00:49:03,171 --> 00:49:06,943
<i>The victims include Chairman Cheon,
head of a major Gangwon construction firm,</i>

725
00:49:06,943 --> 00:49:09,758
<i>and Mr. Tak, the son of a five-term lawmaker.</i>

726
00:49:09,758 --> 00:49:11,811
<i>The two men were together
in Chairman Cheon's room</i>

727
00:49:11,811 --> 00:49:14,075
<i>when a single bullet
fired from outside the window</i>

728
00:49:14,075 --> 00:49:18,091
- <i>instantly killed them both.</i>
- <i>Chairman Cheon is Cheon Seong Gil, right?</i>

729
00:49:18,091 --> 00:49:19,703
This can't be happening.

730
00:49:19,703 --> 00:49:21,291
What's all this?

731
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:23,758
And who's this Mr. Tak
who was killed with him?

732
00:49:23,758 --> 00:49:25,351
<i>Accordingly, the sniper's point of origin...</i>

733
00:49:25,351 --> 00:49:26,924
It's someone I know.

734
00:49:26,924 --> 00:49:28,124
<i>Pardon?</i>

735
00:49:28,124 --> 00:49:31,024
Do you know him? Who is he?

736
00:49:31,024 --> 00:49:34,839
The son of Assemblyman Tak Geun Soo,
Tak Jong Gu.

737
00:49:34,839 --> 00:49:38,399
<i>Given the low-lying hills
outside the windows,</i>

738
00:49:38,399 --> 00:49:41,291
<i>investigators will need to determine</i>

739
00:49:41,291 --> 00:49:43,291
- <i>where Kingfisher carried out the attack.</i>
- Ah, I wanted a chicken leg,

740
00:49:43,291 --> 00:49:44,451
but they're already sold out.

741
00:49:44,451 --> 00:49:46,191
They're really popular these days.

742
00:49:46,191 --> 00:49:49,567
Instead, I got you this fish cake bar
and the cream bread you like.

743
00:49:49,567 --> 00:49:51,427
And I got two sweet Choco Pies.

744
00:49:51,427 --> 00:49:52,659
Here you go!

745
00:49:52,659 --> 00:49:54,359
And some hot coffee!

746
00:49:55,411 --> 00:49:58,358
You were always lecturing me about
not using my phone while we're on stakeout.

747
00:49:58,358 --> 00:49:59,907
So what could be so interesting?

748
00:49:59,907 --> 00:50:01,607
Shh!

749
00:50:04,136 --> 00:50:05,563
[Two Victims Shot with a Single Bullet]

750
00:50:05,587 --> 00:50:08,724
What's this? Kingfisher struck again already?

751
00:50:11,075 --> 00:50:12,387
Two people?

752
00:50:12,387 --> 00:50:14,015
With one bullet?

753
00:50:14,015 --> 00:50:15,651
So, what is it? One shot, two kills?

754
00:50:15,651 --> 00:50:18,691
- Amazing!
- Hey, you're making a racket.

755
00:50:19,671 --> 00:50:20,671
Where are we going?

756
00:50:20,671 --> 00:50:22,827
We're in the middle of a stakeout, aren't we?

757
00:50:22,827 --> 00:50:25,503
Mr. Jang is going to take over.
He'll be here soon.

758
00:50:25,503 --> 00:50:28,075
Oh, so where are we...

759
00:50:28,075 --> 00:50:29,124
[Hongseon Casino]
Hongseon?

760
00:50:29,124 --> 00:50:31,731
A casino? At this hour?

761
00:50:31,731 --> 00:50:33,955
If we want to get footage of the scene,
we have to go now.

762
00:50:33,955 --> 00:50:35,019
Get some sleep.

763
00:50:35,019 --> 00:50:37,243
Wow, the scene of a one-shot double kill.

764
00:50:37,243 --> 00:50:41,024
But if the chief finds out about this,
we'll just get yelled at, right?

765
00:50:52,868 --> 00:50:55,520
[Five Years Ago]
The defendant, Tak Jong Gu,

766
00:50:55,520 --> 00:50:57,881
was found not guilty.

767
00:51:00,181 --> 00:51:03,196
Good work. Why did it take so long?

768
00:51:03,196 --> 00:51:04,624
No, this is unbelievable.

769
00:51:04,624 --> 00:51:08,668
How can there be a verdict like this?

770
00:51:08,668 --> 00:51:10,472
- Mom...
- My daughter is dead!

771
00:51:10,472 --> 00:51:12,415
- My sister...
- That punk killed her!

772
00:51:12,415 --> 00:51:14,956
- Mom!
- Hey!

773
00:51:14,956 --> 00:51:16,656
Mom...

774
00:51:18,456 --> 00:51:19,456
Bring my daughter back!

775
00:51:19,456 --> 00:51:22,428
How can he be found not guilty?

776
00:51:22,428 --> 00:51:25,381
Bring my daughter back!

777
00:51:25,381 --> 00:51:27,948
- Hey!
- Bring her back!

778
00:51:27,948 --> 00:51:29,964
- I said bring my daughter back!
- Mom...

779
00:51:29,964 --> 00:51:32,348
Bring my daughter back!

780
00:51:34,203 --> 00:51:36,193
[Court]

781
00:51:38,776 --> 00:51:41,915
Hey, get everyone together right now.

782
00:51:41,915 --> 00:51:44,952
What do you think? A celebration, you idiot.

783
00:51:44,952 --> 00:51:46,796
The girls?

784
00:51:46,796 --> 00:51:50,408
Of course, we should invite them.

785
00:51:50,408 --> 00:51:52,148
Yeah.

786
00:51:52,148 --> 00:51:53,324
Oh, really?

787
00:51:53,324 --> 00:51:56,015
Then should we just rent out an entire club?

788
00:51:58,816 --> 00:52:00,581
Let's go!

789
00:52:39,908 --> 00:52:42,848
Oh, Bo Na, Bo Na!

790
00:52:44,804 --> 00:52:47,092
Tae Seong!

791
00:52:47,092 --> 00:52:48,392
What brings you here at this hour?

792
00:52:48,392 --> 00:52:50,628
I came because I missed you.

793
00:52:50,628 --> 00:52:56,681
I just really wanted
to see you tonight, Bo Na.

794
00:53:00,016 --> 00:53:02,348
Have you been drinking?

795
00:53:02,348 --> 00:53:04,928
Well... a little?

796
00:53:04,928 --> 00:53:07,164
What...

797
00:53:07,164 --> 00:53:10,020
Why did you drink so much?
You can't even hold your liquor.

798
00:53:10,020 --> 00:53:12,516
That's not true. I can hold my liquor, okay?

799
00:53:12,516 --> 00:53:13,516
Tch...

800
00:53:13,516 --> 00:53:20,140
Still, I'd rather have
a strawberry shake with you.

801
00:53:20,140 --> 00:53:23,648
Cheers! Your favorite strawberry shake.

802
00:53:28,136 --> 00:53:33,164
But today, I just... drank like this.

803
00:53:33,164 --> 00:53:38,348
I drank because the only thing
I could hold in my hand

804
00:53:39,232 --> 00:53:40,940
was a glass of alcohol.

805
00:53:40,940 --> 00:53:45,796
Not a gun, not a knife, not even a pen.

806
00:53:45,796 --> 00:53:49,281
So I ended up with a glass.

807
00:53:56,340 --> 00:53:59,688
Did something happen today?

808
00:53:59,688 --> 00:54:01,740
Something?

809
00:54:01,740 --> 00:54:04,056
Well, yeah...

810
00:54:04,056 --> 00:54:06,668
Something always happens.
It's an everyday thing.

811
00:54:06,668 --> 00:54:08,756
Getting slammed into walls,

812
00:54:08,756 --> 00:54:11,815
thrown to the floor,

813
00:54:12,884 --> 00:54:16,852
and having my heart...

814
00:54:16,852 --> 00:54:19,615
ripped apart?

815
00:54:22,815 --> 00:54:25,481
I don't know what else I'm supposed to do.

816
00:54:30,015 --> 00:54:33,215
Bad people should be punished.

817
00:54:34,752 --> 00:54:37,981
Truly bad people should be punished.

818
00:54:40,948 --> 00:54:42,648
But I...

819
00:54:50,508 --> 00:54:53,315
I can't do anything about it.

820
00:55:31,452 --> 00:55:33,572
Get some sleep on the way.

821
00:55:33,572 --> 00:55:36,281
What are you thinking about so hard?

822
00:55:36,281 --> 00:55:38,316
Oh, nothing.

823
00:55:38,316 --> 00:55:40,784
I was just thinking about a certain day.

824
00:55:40,784 --> 00:55:42,708
What day?

825
00:55:42,708 --> 00:55:45,181
The day my husband cried for the second time.

826
00:55:49,892 --> 00:55:52,320
Well, aren't you tired yourself?

827
00:55:52,320 --> 00:55:56,812
I told you and Manager Go
to take a day off. I can drive.

828
00:55:56,812 --> 00:56:01,136
Ms. Yoo, how could I let you go alone?

829
00:56:01,136 --> 00:56:03,448
Driving at night is dangerous.

830
00:56:06,552 --> 00:56:09,908
Oh, no... I know you're...

831
00:56:09,908 --> 00:56:12,081
an excellent driver.

832
00:56:12,704 --> 00:56:15,215
But still, today...

833
00:56:15,215 --> 00:56:16,915
What about today?

834
00:56:18,704 --> 00:56:21,308
I just couldn't bring myself
to leave you alone.

835
00:56:21,308 --> 00:56:25,016
After the scare we had earlier.

836
00:56:25,016 --> 00:56:26,848
Especially since it was because of me.

837
00:56:27,524 --> 00:56:29,715
Hey, I told you it wasn't your fault.

838
00:56:29,715 --> 00:56:32,415
Unexpected things can happen anytime.

839
00:56:34,515 --> 00:56:36,620
It was the first time, Ms. Yoo.

840
00:56:36,620 --> 00:56:39,615
The first time I was truly scared.
Especially while I was there on-site.

841
00:56:41,392 --> 00:56:43,248
Me too.

842
00:56:43,248 --> 00:56:46,081
I was scared for the first time.

843
00:56:51,164 --> 00:56:54,032
Is this because you saw your husband today?

844
00:56:54,032 --> 00:56:56,648
You seemed bothered by it the whole time.

845
00:56:57,315 --> 00:57:00,381
Why did I never think of it?

846
00:57:01,044 --> 00:57:04,015
That something like this could happen.

847
00:57:43,764 --> 00:57:46,648
It's Yoo Bo Na, my wife.

848
00:57:48,068 --> 00:57:50,348
My big precious.

849
00:57:50,348 --> 00:57:53,248
Sorry, I woke you, right?

850
00:57:54,316 --> 00:57:57,608
I thought you'd be staying the night.

851
00:57:57,608 --> 00:58:00,084
I came back early because I missed you.

852
00:58:00,084 --> 00:58:02,915
I really missed you today.

853
00:58:06,516 --> 00:58:09,515
I missed you so much too.

854
00:58:12,744 --> 00:58:16,424
I'm off tomorrow. Want to go on a date?

855
00:58:16,424 --> 00:58:18,272
Let's do that.

856
00:58:18,272 --> 00:58:22,215
Let's have the date we missed last time.

857
00:58:22,920 --> 00:58:25,848
We'll look at the sky and enjoy the scenery.

858
00:58:27,396 --> 00:58:31,115
We'll worry about what to wear
and what to eat.

859
00:58:33,712 --> 00:58:37,372
Let's just have
an ordinary day together, okay?

860
00:58:37,372 --> 00:58:39,981
Just like the day we first met.

861
00:58:41,308 --> 00:58:43,881
Just like the day we first met.

862
00:58:55,408 --> 00:58:57,544
<i>Why didn't I think of that?</i>

863
00:58:57,544 --> 00:59:00,004
<i>That he's always out there,</i>

864
00:59:00,004 --> 00:59:02,056
<i>and as long as I'm still here,</i>

865
00:59:02,056 --> 00:59:07,281
<i>we could run into each other again
someday, somewhere.</i>

866
00:59:14,548 --> 00:59:16,281
<i>Just like...</i>

867
00:59:16,281 --> 00:59:19,381
<i>the day we first met.</i>

868
00:59:59,502 --> 01:00:03,527
[A Bona Fide Killer]

869
01:00:03,551 --> 01:00:05,724
Back then, everyone was curious
when you came back.

870
01:00:05,724 --> 01:00:07,392
They wondered what had happened
in the meantime.

871
01:00:07,392 --> 01:00:09,348
I met Yoo Bo Na.

872
01:00:09,348 --> 01:00:10,716
Try to stay alive, at least.

873
01:00:10,716 --> 01:00:12,681
Did you save Mr. Kwon Tae Seong?

874
01:00:12,681 --> 01:00:13,681
Because I felt like it.

875
01:00:13,681 --> 01:00:15,744
Have we met before?

876
01:00:15,744 --> 01:00:19,588
How do you keep picking out exactly
the people Kingfisher targets?

877
01:00:19,588 --> 01:00:21,952
But when I think about it,
she's really something.

878
01:00:21,952 --> 01:00:23,868
How on earth has she lived her life?

879
01:00:23,868 --> 01:00:24,964
Do you know anything, Tae Seong?

880
01:00:24,964 --> 01:00:28,460
Why would Director Yoo summon us
to her home herself?

881
01:00:28,460 --> 01:00:29,508
Wait a minute.

882
01:00:29,508 --> 01:00:32,848
Could Kingfisher have killed
an innocent person by mistake?

883
01:00:32,848 --> 01:00:35,268
If an innocent person was killed,
they should be held accountable too.

884
01:00:35,268 --> 01:00:37,081
Kingfisher should be caught
and locked up too.

885
01:00:37,081 --> 01:00:39,188
I got a text from Director Yoo.

886
01:00:39,188 --> 01:00:40,240
What did she say?

887
01:00:40,240 --> 01:00:41,588
I'm quitting.

888
01:00:41,588 --> 01:00:43,648
You used to want so badly to meet Kingfisher.

889
01:00:43,648 --> 01:00:45,581
I shouldn't meet her.
